1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:06,056
Two of the most powerful air forces on earth, built on completely different ideas.

2
00:00:06,056 --> 00:00:09,484
One flies fewer, older, more expensive aircraft.

3
00:00:09,484 --> 00:00:14,054
The other is building faster than anyone has since the Cold War.

4
00:00:14,054 --> 00:00:18,625
Here is every fighter that matters in 2026, compared one by one.

5
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,675
Same sky.

6
00:00:02,675 --> 00:00:05,975
Two answers.

7
00:00:05,975 --> 00:00:18,625
And ten years to find out which one was right.

8
00:00:19,875 --> 00:00:24,307
Start with the aircraft both air forces are built around.

9
00:00:24,307 --> 00:00:29,749
America's F-22 was designed to win a war that never came: supercruise,

10
00:00:29,749 --> 00:00:34,414
thrust vectoring and a radar signature the size of a marble.

11
00:00:34,414 --> 00:00:37,213
China's J-20 is a bigger, later bet.

12
00:00:37,213 --> 00:00:44,366
Canards, two engines, and long-range missiles meant to hit tankers and radar planes from far

13
00:00:44,366 --> 00:00:45,765
outside the fight.

14
00:00:46,565 --> 00:00:51,023
The F-35 is the opposite idea: instead of one perfect fighter,

15
00:00:51,023 --> 00:00:56,847
build one airframe in enormous numbers and let software make it several aircraft.

16
00:00:56,847 --> 00:01:03,102
China's answer is the J-35, a smaller stealth fighter aimed at carrier decks and export

17
00:01:03,102 --> 00:01:03,821
customers.

18
00:01:03,821 --> 00:01:08,566
It is years behind in numbers — and that gap is the whole contest.

19
00:01:09,366 --> 00:01:14,163
Stealth opens the door; these two carry the bombs through it.

20
00:01:14,163 --> 00:01:21,318
The F-15EX is the oldest design in this film and still carries the most: thirteen tonnes of

21
00:01:21,318 --> 00:01:25,564
munitions and hypersonic missiles the F-35 cannot fit.

22
00:01:25,564 --> 00:01:29,889
China's J-16 is the same idea built around the Flanker,

23
00:01:29,889 --> 00:01:33,585
with a strike radar and a long anti-ship reach.

24
00:01:34,385 --> 00:01:40,212
Both countries kept buying light fighters for the same reason: you can afford a thousand of

25
00:01:40,212 --> 00:01:40,532
them.

26
00:01:40,532 --> 00:01:44,374
The Viper has been upgraded for forty years and still sells.

27
00:01:44,374 --> 00:01:48,857
The J-10C is China's first genuinely independent design in this class,

28
00:01:48,857 --> 00:01:52,763
with an active electronically scanned radar and a delta wing.

29
00:01:53,563 --> 00:01:55,858
Here is the number that matters.

30
00:01:55,858 --> 00:02:02,024
America flies roughly twenty-four hundred combat aircraft; China roughly two thousand.

31
00:02:02,024 --> 00:02:07,617
The US has held that lead for decades, but it is not growing — and China's is,

32
00:02:07,617 --> 00:02:10,270
by around a hundred airframes a year.

33
00:02:11,070 --> 00:02:13,172
On stealth the gap is much wider.

34
00:02:13,172 --> 00:02:18,203
The United States has delivered well over a thousand fifth-generation fighters.

35
00:02:18,203 --> 00:02:23,999
China has built somewhere near three hundred J-20s — the largest non-American stealth fleet

36
00:02:23,999 --> 00:02:26,674
in the world, and the one growing fastest.

37
00:02:27,474 --> 00:02:31,936
An aircraft carrier of the sky is an early warning radar.

38
00:02:31,936 --> 00:02:36,632
America is retiring the E-3 and moving to the E-7 Wedgetail,

39
00:02:36,632 --> 00:02:39,215
a fixed AESA beam on an airliner.

40
00:02:39,215 --> 00:02:43,990
China built the KJ-500 for the job, fifty of them in service,

41
00:02:43,990 --> 00:02:47,513
with a radome the size of a destroyer's mast.

42
00:02:48,313 --> 00:02:49,951
This is the quiet one.

43
00:02:49,951 --> 00:02:55,464
America's refuelling fleet turns every fighter into a long-range aircraft,

44
00:02:55,464 --> 00:02:58,369
and it operates across the whole world.

45
00:02:58,369 --> 00:03:05,223
China's YY-20 is new, small, and built for a fight near home — which is exactly the fight it

46
00:03:05,223 --> 00:03:05,670
plans.

47
00:03:06,470 --> 00:03:07,390
So who wins?

48
00:03:07,390 --> 00:03:09,000
Neither, in a number.

49
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:15,287
America has more aircraft, more tankers, more combat hours and allies to fly from.

50
00:03:15,287 --> 00:03:19,580
China has the newest fleet, the fastest production line,

51
00:03:19,580 --> 00:03:23,414
and the advantage of fighting in its own airspace.

52
00:03:23,414 --> 00:03:29,701
The honest answer is that the gap is narrowing — and the next ten years decide it.

